{"review":"approved","flags":[{"page":15,"note":"The side note writes '−1(wᵀxᵢ + b) ≤ 1'; it should be '(wᵀxᵢ + b) ≤ −1' (equivalently −1·(wᵀxᵢ + b) ≥ 1)."},{"page":77,"note":"α₁ = α₂ is printed as 0.859; the correct value is 0.0859 (= 11/128), which the slide itself uses on p.78."},{"page":79,"note":"b = −1.2501/0.1243 = −10.057 is a rounding artefact; exact arithmetic gives w̃ = (1/8, 1/8, −5/4) and b = −10."},{"page":36,"note":"The augmented-vector shortcut regularises b and drops Σαᵢyᵢ = 0 (here Σαᵢyᵢ = −2). It gives the correct boundary in this example, verified with scikit-learn."},{"page":66,"note":"'If d is a distance then exp(−d) is a kernel' is not true for every metric (it holds e.g. for Euclidean distance squared or L1 distance); kept as on the slide with this caveat."}],"recall":{"defs":[["Support vector machine","Maximum-margin classifier."],["Support vector","Training point with α > 0 (on/inside the margin)."],["Slack variable","Amount by which a point violates its margin."],["Kernel","Inner product in a feature space computed directly."],["KKT conditions","Optimality conditions with inequality constraints."],["Hinge loss","max(0, 1 − y f(x))."]],"formulas":["M=\\frac{2}{\\|\\mathbf w\\|}","\\min\\tfrac12\\|\\mathbf w\\|^2+C\\sum\\xi_i\\ \\text{s.t.}\\ y_i(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x_i+b)\\ge1-\\xi_i","\\max_\\alpha\\sum\\alpha_i-\\tfrac12\\sum_{i,j}\\alpha_i\\alpha_jy_iy_jK(\\mathbf x_i,\\mathbf x_j)","f(\\mathbf x)=\\operatorname{sign}\\Big(\\sum\\alpha_iy_iK(\\mathbf x_i,\\mathbf x)+b\\Big)","K_{RBF}=\\exp(-\\|\\mathbf x-\\mathbf z\\|^2/2\\sigma^2)"],"takeaways":["Maximum margin = minimum ½‖w‖² under y(wᵀx + b) ≥ 1.","KKT: only support vectors have α > 0; w = Σαᵢyᵢxᵢ.","Soft margin: slack, hinge loss, C trades margin vs errors.","Kernels replace dot products to give non-linear boundaries.","Multi-class via one-vs-all or one-vs-one."],"confused":[["Hard vs soft margin","No violations vs penalised slack."],["C vs γ","Violation penalty vs kernel width."],["Hinge vs log loss","Zero beyond margin vs always positive."],["OvA vs OvO","C models vs C(C − 1)/2 models."]],"minute":"An SVM finds the separating hyperplane with the largest margin. With margins at wᵀx + b = ±1, the width is 2/‖w‖, so it minimises ½‖w‖² subject to yᵢ(wᵀxᵢ + b) ≥ 1, a convex quadratic program. Lagrange multipliers and KKT give the dual, which depends only on dot products, and show that only support vectors have α > 0, with w = Σαᵢyᵢxᵢ. Soft margins add slack penalised by C via the hinge loss. Kernels such as polynomial and RBF replace dot products to give non-linear boundaries, and multiple classes use one-vs-all or one-vs-one."},"flashcards":[["Linear classifier","$f=\\operatorname{sign}(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x+b)$",4],["Support vectors","Points on the margin; removing them moves the hyperplane",12],["Margin width","$2/\\|\\mathbf w\\|$",13],["Hard-margin primal","$\\min\\tfrac12\\|\\mathbf w\\|^2$ s.t. $y_i(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x_i+b)\\ge1$",15],["Lagrange condition","$\\nabla f=\\lambda\\nabla g$",24],["KKT complementary slackness","$\\mu_j^*h_j(\\mathbf x^*)=0$",28],["Dual objective","$\\sum\\alpha_i-\\tfrac12\\sum\\alpha_i\\alpha_jy_iy_j\\mathbf x_i^T\\mathbf x_j$",30],["w from α","$\\mathbf w=\\sum\\alpha_iy_i\\mathbf x_i$",32],["Soft margin","$\\tfrac12\\|\\mathbf w\\|^2+C\\sum\\xi_i$, $y_if\\ge1-\\xi_i$",45],["Hinge loss","$\\max(0,1-yf(\\mathbf x))$",43],["Large C","Small margin, fewer training errors",46],["Kernel","$K(\\mathbf x_i,\\mathbf x_j)=\\phi(\\mathbf x_i)^T\\phi(\\mathbf x_j)$",58],["RBF kernel","$\\exp(-\\|\\mathbf x_i-\\mathbf x_j\\|^2/2\\sigma^2)$",60],["Mercer conditions","Continuous, symmetric, positive semi-definite",65],["One-vs-one","$C(C-1)/2$ classifiers, majority vote",89]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["s-linear"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what","h2"],"deep":["s-margin"],"viz":["widestRoad"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["s-sv"],"viz":["svmPlayground"],"status":"comple